# xftest4.input — open the File menu on a borderless form, choose Quit.
#
# The form is 300x200.  The File touch menu is at (20,20) 80x25, so press at its
# centre (60,32).  While the button is held the menu shell drops down as an
# override-redirect popup; the compositor then delivers subsequent coordinates
# to *that* surface, so the release is popup-relative.  The single "Quit" item
# sits at the bottom of the 95x54 shell, around (47,40).
#
# There is deliberately no trailing "screenshot": the compositor exits the
# instant it takes one, closing the Wayland connection while the client may still
# be handling the selection, and the client would die of XIO rather than printing
# its marker and exiting 0.

motion 60 32
sleep 300
button press left
sleep 500
motion 47 40
sleep 300
button release left
sleep 800
